    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d291">

                <pb facs="0454" n="374" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg374"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Mutual Guarantee (Locarno)/851</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1080</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-12-03">December 3,
                        1936</date>.<lb/>[Received December 11.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Embassy’s despatch No.
                    1036, of October 26, 1936,<anchor n="27" xml:id="d291-f1"/> concerning Belgian
                    Foreign Policy and the Locarno negotiations, I have the honor to report that the
                    Belgian Government has received from the British Government two further notes
                    dated November 4, 1936, and November 19, 1936, regarding the question of a new
                    Western Pact. Mr. Le Ghait, <hi rendition="#italic">Chef de Cabinet</hi> of the
                    Belgian Minister for Foreign Affairs, informed a member of the Embassy (Mr.
                    Sussdorff) yesterday that the Belgian Government is now drafting its reply to
                    the last two British notes. Mr. Le Ghait said that it was not possible to give a
                    synopsis of the Belgian reply yet, as the reply <pb facs="0455" n="375"
                        xml:id="pg375"/> will not be ready until next week, but he intimated that it
                    will be entirely favorable and in line with the desires of the British
                    Government. A memorandum of this conversation is enclosed.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dave H. Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d291-a1.xml" xpointer="d291-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
